# Multi-disc pass-through: a 0-byte .m3u stub downloads via the SAME wrap path; the engine
# owns the multi-disc shape (populated .m3u + discs in the dot-hidden per-game folder —
# never a bare disc at the Roms root) and the stock launcher gets the .m3u.
desc fetch: multi-disc .m3u stub -> engine folder-per-game shape, launches the .m3u
invoke wrap
tag PS
romarg Roms/PS/ChronoCross.m3u
config paired
wifi up
sdfile Roms/PS/ChronoCross.m3u
engine 0|RESULT downloaded=1 discs_present=1
engine 0|LOCAL=none
engine 0|RESULT mode=list-states n=0
expect_exit 0
expect_trace ENGINE --download
expect_file_has Roms/PS/ChronoCross.m3u (Disc 1)
expect_file Roms/PS/.ChronoCross/ChronoCross (Disc 1).chd
expect_trace STOCK PS rom=
expect_trace ChronoCross.m3u'
